ath-academy-id "q-87262" :question/problem "Given that $P(A)=0.5,$ $P(A\\cap B)=0.4,$ and $P(A\\cup B)=0.8,$ find $P({B}^{′}).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $P(B)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ 0.8 & =0.5+P(B)-0.4 \\\\ P(B) & =0.8+0.4-0.5 \\\\ P(B) & =0.7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P({B}^{′}) & =1-P(B) \\\\  & =1-0.7 \\\\  & =0.3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-87262/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "44603ff6-f9c7-5a02-83c1-0e803444bd25"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-87262"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-179539/selection/0417788a5409ad5447fb6d379532fc1bfef99c80e1411a914d6ff9762ba8f7ac" :answer/id #uuid "52c78070-3a7e-52fa-95cb-712b749aa21f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-179539/selection/3089f9a34f7a805d8b2b2d5d51b10dc7aea027e8ec8fd8d06ad11cecf2ba9740" :answer/id #uuid "a301ec8c-bf6b-5c14-9f67-9a616b6f6135" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-179539/selection/ea886782f883139045e5abc122fc35c608bfcc0ac4d51b469ff658e915045408" :answer/id #uuid "6bdf0f46-e510-57fb-9196-c84f08486ee6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-179539/selection/c7e2c99672184a6ffc5fe21255ac37862a4c27e4b225c7b645ba47d8f3c76eda" :answer/id #uuid "93751f4d-3d21-5cc9-bf2a-b1f1a2772bcc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-179539/selection/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903" :answer/id #uuid "5cfff7ee-5653-54e1-9d64-a27f7e4bfa05" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-179539/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8648fee5-2807-506e-9132-b7540548afdc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-179539/selection/3089f9a34f7a805d8b2b2d5d51b10dc7aea027e8ec8fd8d06ad11cecf2ba9740" :answer-field/choices ["q-179539/selection/0417788a5409ad5447fb6d379532fc1bfef99c80e1411a914d6ff9762ba8f7ac" "q-179539/selection/3089f9a34f7a805d8b2b2d5d51b10dc7aea027e8ec8fd8d06ad11cecf2ba9740" "q-179539/selection/ea886782f883139045e5abc122fc35c608bfcc0ac4d51b469ff658e915045408" "q-179539/selection/c7e2c99672184a6ffc5fe21255ac37862a4c27e4b225c7b645ba47d8f3c76eda" "q-179539/selection/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-179539" :question/id #uuid "5fe77a5c-4312-5b94-9b61-405a56afc897" :question/math-academy-id "q-179539" :question/problem "Given that $P(A)=\\frac{1}{2},$ $P(B)=\\frac{2}{5},$ and $P(A\\cup B)=\\frac{7}{10},$ find $P(A\\cup {B}^{′}).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $P(A\\cap B)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ \\frac{7}{10} & =\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{2}{5}-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ P(A\\cap B) & =\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{2}{5}-\\frac{7}{10} \\\\ P(A\\cap B) & =\\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we construct the corresponding Venn diagram and shade the region $A\\cup {B}^{′}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064054/assets/5ecc7dae3e6b6e57ccd4a7b8907cb4dd20b0ece400a5768b747f3cb3da788e4b.png)\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nP(A\\cup {B}^{′})=\\frac{3}{10}+\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{3}{10}=\\frac{4}{5}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-179539/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "053ab8bb-73ba-54b1-b195-05d4e12c56f1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-179539"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-264403/field-1/a44ed9268297050614edc4097a04d3089044bc70b376ad604b0445193a602b0a" :answer/id #uuid "a088d687-f56b-5771-86ee-ba5215245646" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.65" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-264403/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "53855a49-5e83-52e8-a0e4-3c60ff6a5cd8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-264403/field-1/a44ed9268297050614edc4097a04d3089044bc70b376ad604b0445193a602b0a" :answer-field/choices ["q-264403/field-1/a44ed9268297050614edc4097a04d3089044bc70b376ad604b0445193a602b0a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-264403" :question/id #uuid "afce1321-9dc1-5a34-b2c6-72efabe0368c" :question/math-academy-id "q-264403" :question/problem "Given that $P(A)=0.25,$ $P(B)=0.45,$ and $P(A\\cup B)=0.6,$ find $P(A\\cup {B}^{′}).$\n\n$P(A\\cup {B}^{′})=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $P(A\\cap B)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ 0.6 & =0.25+0.45-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ P(A\\cap B) & =0.25+0.45-0.6 \\\\  & =0.1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we construct the corresponding Venn diagram and shade the region $A\\cup {B}^{′}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14064054/assets/f8fb716593a35fc1f85ab524dc78bf0fa0cd03dc16b0c5ca92a9b2836e6e7c5b.png)\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\nP(A\\cup {B}^{′})=0.15+0.1+0.4=0.65.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-264403/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "053ab8bb-73ba-54b1-b195-05d4e12c56f1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-264403"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-264416/field-1/95a1d5fa369c4d08bda10228102d0fbae8f93732afc4c2ec3773c4f3d47df28c" :answer/id #uuid "43ba118a-6d5e-5035-ae23-fb3680b5ae34" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-264416/field-1/5d227958e8e2ab9feb7a492bded665cf59dfa9121f7d82334971c99adf799e26" :answer/id #uuid "346a03b2-edfe-57d2-aece-c0791f822b6e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-264416/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e3d64430-ebc6-5724-be8e-77d588adbd85" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-264416/field-1/95a1d5fa369c4d08bda10228102d0fbae8f93732afc4c2ec3773c4f3d47df28c" :answer-field/choices ["q-264416/field-1/95a1d5fa369c4d08bda10228102d0fbae8f93732afc4c2ec3773c4f3d47df28c" "q-264416/field-1/5d227958e8e2ab9feb7a492bded665cf59dfa9121f7d82334971c99adf799e26"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-264416" :question/id #uuid "c1421b79-b763-507f-bc9d-72470c20c64a" :question/math-academy-id "q-264416" :question/problem "Given that $P(B)=0.45,$ $P(A\\cap B)=0.2,$ and $P(A\\cup B)=0.75,$ find $P({A}^{′}).$\n\n$P({A}^{′})=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $P(A)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ 0.75 & =P(A)+0.45-0.2 \\\\ P(A) & =0.75+0.2-0.45 \\\\  & =0.5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P({A}^{′}) & =1-P(A) \\\\  & =1-0.5 \\\\  & =0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-264416/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "44603ff6-f9c7-5a02-83c1-0e803444bd25"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-264416"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-264424/field-1/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903" :answer/id #uuid "8128fbed-1512-5c5c-a0b0-b281928ce934" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-264424/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "78a12c31-13a3-5cb7-9c7d-1c91bc8cee33" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-264424/field-1/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903" :answer-field/choices ["q-264424/field-1/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-264424" :question/id #uuid "fea666e2-5052-54f2-889f-1e9563ba7916" :question/math-academy-id "q-264424" :question/problem "Given that $P(B)=\\frac{4}{15},$ $P(A\\cap B)=\\frac{1}{15},$ and $P(A\\cup B)=\\frac{4}{5},$ find $P({A}^{′}).$\n\n$P({A}^{′})=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate $P(A)$ using the addition law:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A\\cup B) & =P(A)+P(B)-P(A\\cap B) \\\\ \\frac{4}{5} & =P(A)+\\frac{4}{15}-\\frac{1}{15} \\\\ P(A) & =\\frac{4}{5}+\\frac{1}{15}-\\frac{4}{15} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P({A}^{′}) & =1-P(A) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{3}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-264424/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "44603ff6-f9c7-5a02-83c1-0e803444bd25"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-264424"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
